VeridianOS: fix kdeplasma-addons compiler warnings

GCC reported:
- applets/comic/engine/comic.cpp:100,108 -Wmissing-field-initializers (15
  members each): the error results were built as
  ComicMetaData{.reason = reason, .error = true}. The surrounding
  QT_WARNING_DISABLE_*("-Wmissing-designated-field-initializers") pragmas
  name a different option, so they never covered GCC's warning. The error
  result is now built by a local lambda that value-initializes the struct
  (ComicMetaData data{}) and then assigns reason and error; the pragmas are
  dropped. Every other member gets the same default as before.
- applets/grouping/groupingcontainment.cpp:74 -Wunused-variable: the
  oldContainmentInstantiated flag was set and never read; removed.
- applets/weather/weatherdatamonitor_p.cpp:236 -Wmissing-field-initializers
  (IonInfo::forecastDataList): the designated initializer named only
  ionControl. Now IonInfo info{} followed by assigning ionControl; the other
  members keep their defaults (locationCount 0, empty list). The local lost
  its const, which nothing relied on (it is only copied into the hash).

Behaviour is unchanged.

diff -ru a/applets/comic/engine/comic.cpp b/applets/comic/engine/comic.cpp
